From: Bale <noreply@example.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Sep 2025 09:53:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] macOS: include libgen.h for basename

On macOS (Darwin), `basename` is declared in <libgen.h>. Without this
include, the build fails with an implicit declaration error and an
incompatible integer-to-pointer conversion when assigning to `char *`.

--- a/tools/attr.c
+++ b/tools/attr.c
@@
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <locale.h>
+#include <libgen.h>
 
 #include <attr/attributes.h>
 
 #include "misc.h"
 
 #define	SETOP		1		/* do a SET operation */

